1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,800
Jin,

2
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:02,300
I really like you.

3
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,490
You know how hot Jin is, right?

4
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:07,280
You've been practicing hard all day,

5
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,800
so I bought you some water.

6
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:09,940
Are you...

7
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:11,440
really serious about my friend?

8
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:13,580
Does it look like I'm not?

9
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:15,020
I told you to pretend to flirt with me.

10
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:16,180
Don't get too into it.

11
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,740
I mean, I don't like pretending.

12
00:00:17,770 --> 00:00:19,610
If you have something to say, just say it.

13
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:21,900
I'm going to hit on you for real.

14
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:24,500
No pretending this time.

15
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:28,690
I'd like to dedicate this award to all of you.

16
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,410
How honorable is
that trophy of yours anyway?

17
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:32,630
Do you even realize

18
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:35,490
that you're the real problem in this family?

19
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,310
I do.

20
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:38,730
To you, someone only counts as family

21
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:41,340
if they're useful to you, and that's it.

22
00:00:41,990 --> 00:00:42,820
Honey...

23
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:45,390
Do you think my dad
will ever be able to accept me?

24
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:49,040
I just feel like
I'll never get to be myself

25
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:50,540
as long as I'm still in this world.

26
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:52,510
It's because you never cared about him.

27
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:54,340
If there's anything else I can do
to help with Anda,

28
00:00:54,370 --> 00:00:55,140
let me know.

29
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:56,800
I'm really not crying.

30
00:00:56,830 --> 00:00:59,720
I know. Why don't you go wash up
in my room first?

31
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,860
What are you looking at?

32
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,640
Someone who isn't crying.

33
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:17,320
You're quite the teaser, aren't you?

34
00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:26,910
My friend just died.

35
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:28,740
Just let me cry.

36
00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:32,960
I think of him every time I'm driving.

37
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:38,140
Jin.

38
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:41,140
You might not know this,

39
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:44,800
but I really like Anda as an actor.

40
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,880
He was my source of happiness.

41
00:01:51,479 --> 00:01:53,020
I felt sad when people criticized him.

42
00:01:53,789 --> 00:01:55,340
I felt happy when they praised him.

43
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,240
When this happened to him,

44
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,520
I could barely stand it.

45
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:06,600
If you're sad, you can just show it.

46
00:02:07,470 --> 00:02:09,690
You don't have to worry
about how anyone sees you.

47
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:14,440
He was your best friend after all.

48
00:02:15,730 --> 00:02:17,040
Everyone understands you.

49
00:02:19,550 --> 00:02:21,010
Can I give you a hug?

50
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:54,400
♫When we happened to hold hands,
was that when it all started?♫

51
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:59,420
♫When I somehow memorized your number,
was that when you took my heart?♫

52
00:02:59,840 --> 00:03:04,180
♫Never knew you'd have my heart from the start♫

53
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,620
♫But today...♫

54
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:10,340
What are you guys doing?

55
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:15,240
I'm just stretching.

56
00:03:25,280 --> 00:03:27,690
[The depicted characters, behaviors, locations,
organizations, professions, and events]

57
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:29,550
[are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.]

58
00:03:29,579 --> 00:03:31,610
[It is not intended to endorse or promote
any of the actions or behavior depicted.]

59
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,820
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

60
00:03:45,550 --> 00:03:51,220
♫I used to wonder what we were,♫

61
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:57,870
♫I thought love needed something clearer,♫

62
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:03,950
♫Took me time to learn what really matters♫

63
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:10,630
♫Love has no rules, whatever comes after♫

64
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:17,430
♫As long as I know what my heart wants to find,♫

65
00:04:17,829 --> 00:04:20,350
♫As long as you're standing by my side,♫

66
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:23,670
♫With you, the only one I'd choose every time,♫

67
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:27,540
♫I don't need a reason, as long as you're mine♫

68
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:30,490
♫As long as you hold my hand,♫

69
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,710
♫As long as next to me is where you stand,♫

70
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:37,070
♫You're the one I'll always try to understand,♫

71
00:04:37,090 --> 00:04:40,890
♫No matter how hard the road may be,♫

72
00:04:41,470 --> 00:04:43,950
♫Just hold my hand, and we'll be free♫

73
00:04:44,710 --> 00:04:47,350
♫As long as you're here with me♫

74
00:05:43,610 --> 00:05:44,560
Point B.

75
00:05:45,900 --> 00:05:47,280
1.462...

76
00:05:48,690 --> 00:05:49,440
62...

77
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:51,110
0.132...

78
00:05:51,610 --> 00:05:53,409
So, what actually happened, Jin?

79
00:05:54,400 --> 00:05:55,970
Was it really a murder?

80
00:05:58,870 --> 00:05:59,790
I don't know.

81
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:02,420
I only know as much as you guys do.

82
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:05,400
People on the internet
are just guessing away.

83
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:07,600
But I think there's some truth to the idea

84
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:09,860
that Anda might not have taken his life.

85
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:12,200
Yeah.

86
00:06:12,730 --> 00:06:14,740
I don't think he did it, either.

87
00:06:15,170 --> 00:06:16,450
That's Anda we're talking about.

88
00:06:16,850 --> 00:06:18,050
Our friend, Anda.

89
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:21,140
Jin,

90
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:23,380
what do you think?

91
00:06:27,250 --> 00:06:29,010
He definitely didn't take his life.

92
00:06:29,710 --> 00:06:30,800
That's all I know.

93
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:39,280
Hey!

94
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:42,810
Got bored of your phone or something?

95
00:06:43,050 --> 00:06:44,290
You just tossed it away.

96
00:06:44,530 --> 00:06:47,180
Well, you just showed up out of nowhere.

97
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,720
- You startled me.
- I was calling you from way over there.

98
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:51,320
You were sitting here spacing out.

99
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:59,290
You're allowed to grieve over Anda's death,

100
00:06:59,310 --> 00:07:01,880
but don't waste your feelings
on those crazy people online.

101
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:05,840
I don't want to overthink it,

102
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:08,650
but have you seen what they're saying?

103
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:11,700
They're saying
Anda was just trying to get attention.

104
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:13,480
See?

105
00:07:13,890 --> 00:07:16,720
That's what I meant. Give it to me.

106
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:19,950
I know you're sad,

107
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,450
but there's nothing we can do.

108
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,970
Do you understand, Podduang?

109
00:07:24,070 --> 00:07:25,020
Why?

110
00:07:26,350 --> 00:07:27,620
He was in so much pain.

111
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:30,730
Why did his life have to end like this?

112
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,200
Even after he's gone,

113
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:35,520
people still won't stop hurting him.

114
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:36,980
I understand,

115
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:38,950
but there's nothing we can do.

116
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,290
Let me see.

117
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:42,770
Are you crying?

118
00:07:44,050 --> 00:07:45,290
I'm not.

119
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:47,520
Look at you.

120
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:48,920
We're the same age,

121
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,700
but why do I feel like you're still a kid?

122
00:07:52,490 --> 00:07:53,970
Maybe it's because you're big.

123
00:07:54,210 --> 00:07:55,210
Is that an insult?

124
00:07:55,630 --> 00:07:56,909
I'm your best friend, you know.

125
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:06,240
Return this for me.

126
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:08,230
Thanks a lot, Dunk.

127
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,270
Here, have something sweet.

128
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:14,250
Anyway, this helps.

129
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:17,380
Every time she sends me a screenshot,
the battery is in the red.

130
00:08:18,610 --> 00:08:20,390
But wait...

131
00:08:21,190 --> 00:08:22,660
There are kiosks everywhere.

132
00:08:22,970 --> 00:08:25,830
I borrowed it for you,
and now I have to return it?

133
00:08:26,370 --> 00:08:28,430
Why? Can't you just do that for me?

134
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:31,120
Fine, I will.

135
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:34,240
What are you smiling at?

136
00:08:34,570 --> 00:08:36,460
Yeah, you've been smiling for a while now.

137
00:08:37,909 --> 00:08:38,960
It's just that...

138
00:08:39,350 --> 00:08:42,110
I'm glad to have you two as my friends.

139
00:09:14,090 --> 00:09:15,680
Oh, is something the matter?

140
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:23,320
I didn't see you at lunch,
so I came up to check on you.

141
00:09:23,340 --> 00:09:25,940
And you're not eating?

142
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,750
If you were in my shoes,
would you be able to eat anything?

143
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:37,080
My brother just died.

144
00:09:37,950 --> 00:09:39,990
If you're not feeling up to it,
you can take a break.

145
00:09:40,690 --> 00:09:43,430
I'll take care of this case myself.
Don't worry.

146
00:09:44,910 --> 00:09:45,720
And...

147
00:09:46,750 --> 00:09:48,000
did you find anything else?

148
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:52,480
I'm going through the CCTV footage.

149
00:09:53,470 --> 00:09:55,520
He parked in a very secluded spot,

150
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:56,800
so I have to check it thoroughly.

151
00:09:57,570 --> 00:09:58,220
Anyway,

152
00:09:58,770 --> 00:10:00,840
the forensic report says
he died of suffocation.

153
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:03,440
Did your brother
often fall asleep in the car?

154
00:10:05,380 --> 00:10:06,120
Yes.

155
00:10:07,050 --> 00:10:08,770
When he was sleepy,
he tended to just pass out.

156
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:14,010
Actually, my mom had warned him about it.

157
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,330
I'm being serious here.

158
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:24,930
You also think
this doesn't look like suicide, right?

159
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,480
Yeah, I've been thinking the same thing.

160
00:10:39,350 --> 00:10:42,790
I know that depression is unpredictable,

161
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:45,840
but I don't think that's the case here

162
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:51,170
even though he had to
take sleeping pills regularly.

163
00:10:52,370 --> 00:10:53,240
That's right.

164
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:57,700
They found that it was
a very mild type of sleeping pill,

165
00:10:58,030 --> 00:11:00,200
and there wasn't a large amount
in his system.

166
00:11:04,810 --> 00:11:07,210
I was actually the last person to see him.

167
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:12,860
Why did I let him drive all by himself?

168
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:16,590
Where did you part ways with your brother?

169
00:11:20,570 --> 00:11:21,920
At a restaurant near our house.

170
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:24,650
As I said,

171
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:27,030
Anda moved out to live in a condo,

172
00:11:28,310 --> 00:11:31,640
so I had to make plans
to meet up with him and catch up.

173
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,750
He seemed perfectly fine, though.

174
00:11:35,730 --> 00:11:37,490
We were both acting very normal.

175
00:11:38,810 --> 00:11:40,140
I was even complaining to him

176
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:43,550
about how he used my car
but wouldn't go get it washed.

177
00:11:47,610 --> 00:11:48,770
Why?

178
00:11:50,470 --> 00:11:52,040
What happened, Lieutenant?

179
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:54,130
Itti,

180
00:11:55,570 --> 00:11:56,790
I promise you

181
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:58,800
that if someone is behind this incident,

182
00:11:59,050 --> 00:12:00,930
I'll make sure they end up behind bars.

183
00:12:02,270 --> 00:12:03,400
You don't have to worry at all.

184
00:12:03,730 --> 00:12:06,010
My team and I
are willing to do our best for you.

185
00:12:07,050 --> 00:12:08,320
Thank you very much, Lieutenant.

186
00:12:09,770 --> 00:12:12,160
If you find out where he went
after parting ways with me

187
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,710
or who he met,

188
00:12:14,810 --> 00:12:15,970
please report it to me.

189
00:12:18,390 --> 00:12:20,060
I might be able to provide some information.

190
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:22,520
My family and I

191
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:24,550
will cooperate fully.

192
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,140
Of course.

193
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:45,480
Stop reading the comments on Anda's news.

194
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,970
These netizens are just talking nonsense.

195
00:12:50,010 --> 00:12:51,620
It's not like there are many.

196
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:54,770
Most of them are just asking
about the cause of death.

197
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:56,590
What do you think, though?

198
00:12:57,810 --> 00:13:00,010
Do you think Anda was murdered?

199
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,280
On today's topic,

200
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,950
- regarding actor Anda's death,
- I think...

201
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:07,700
- it's possible that he was murdered.
- police are currently investigating

202
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:10,380
to determine the cause of death
and establish what happened.

203
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:13,260
Preliminary forensic findings indicate that

204
00:13:13,350 --> 00:13:16,360
the cause of death

205
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,680
may have been suffocation.

206
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:22,680
However, authorities are continuing
to examine the evidence

207
00:13:22,710 --> 00:13:24,200
and gather further details

208
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:27,730
to conclude the cause of death.

209
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:36,860
Oh...

210
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:38,710
Amp, are you taking out the trash?

211
00:13:40,310 --> 00:13:41,060
Oh...

212
00:13:44,170 --> 00:13:44,930
Yes.

213
00:13:49,350 --> 00:13:52,040
Are you okay, Amp?

214
00:13:58,490 --> 00:14:00,430
Anda didn't take his life.

215
00:14:06,990 --> 00:14:08,930
Anda didn't kill himself.

216
00:14:10,650 --> 00:14:11,720
It's true!

217
00:14:12,670 --> 00:14:13,880
We need to help him.

218
00:14:13,910 --> 00:14:15,500
Find the culprit.

219
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:18,700
We need to help Anda. We must help him.

220
00:14:35,810 --> 00:14:37,590
She was talking like she was out of it.

221
00:14:37,830 --> 00:14:39,430
Then she suddenly ran into her room.

222
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,480
I didn't even get to ask her anything.

223
00:14:42,150 --> 00:14:43,320
I'm so confused.

224
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:47,100
She's a fan,
so she must be grieving, too.

225
00:14:47,130 --> 00:14:48,980
That's why she's been acting a bit off.

226
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,890
I'm a fan, too.

227
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:53,340
I've been moping all day.

228
00:14:55,530 --> 00:14:56,410
Podduang,

229
00:14:57,850 --> 00:14:59,030
do you also think

230
00:14:59,270 --> 00:15:00,730
that Anda was murdered?

231
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:04,340
Yeah, I think so, too.

232
00:15:06,110 --> 00:15:09,310
How about we find out the truth together?

233
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:12,150
What truth?

234
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:14,880
The truth about...

235
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:17,300
who actually killed him.

236
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:21,590
Please, Podduang.

237
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:23,690
Help me find them.

238
00:15:24,310 --> 00:15:26,000
Consider it a final favor for Anda.

239
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,600
Yeah, let's help Anda.

240
00:15:48,730 --> 00:15:49,570
Podduang,

241
00:15:50,670 --> 00:15:52,020
have you eaten anything?

242
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:54,400
I have.

243
00:15:55,130 --> 00:15:56,570
And have you slept at all?

244
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:59,450
I have.

245
00:16:06,110 --> 00:16:07,980
It's the one I borrowed.

246
00:16:11,790 --> 00:16:13,460
And you just bought a new one?

247
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,280
Yeah.

248
00:16:14,710 --> 00:16:17,660
I lost yours,
so I bought a new one to replace it.

249
00:16:20,990 --> 00:16:22,510
You guys don't have to worry about me.

250
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,880
I can eat and sleep,

251
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:27,900
but...

252
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,930
I just can't stop thinking about it.

253
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:34,920
How can I help you?

254
00:16:49,770 --> 00:16:50,630
Bumm...

255
00:16:57,910 --> 00:16:58,900
What the hell is this?

256
00:17:00,710 --> 00:17:01,540
What is it?

257
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,700
What the hell is this?

258
00:17:14,890 --> 00:17:16,190
[Breaking! Leaked Messages of Deceased Star
May Hold Clues to His Death]

259
00:17:16,210 --> 00:17:17,349
[Let's break up, Anda.]
[What happened, Kum? What's wrong?]

260
00:17:17,369 --> 00:17:18,730
[I'm sorry, Anda.]
[Kum, you're not like this. What's wrong?]

261
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,020
[Let's break up, Anda.]

262
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:32,160
[Does anyone know Anda's boyfriend? Who is he?]
[Is the chat real or edited?]

263
00:17:32,190 --> 00:17:34,810
[Is Kum involved in Anda's death?]
[Stop guessing blindly, please.]

264
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:37,470
[What do you mean blindly? They broke up
on the day he died. Is that a coincidence?]

265
00:17:37,490 --> 00:17:40,210
[Was this the reason he took his own life?]
[Please respect the deceased and the family.]

266
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:43,370
Is that chat real?

267
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,860
Is this person named Kum
involved in this matter?

268
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,370
I only know as much as you do.

269
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,500
And what do you think?

270
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:53,990
I don't think it was Kum.

271
00:17:55,390 --> 00:17:56,810
Why are you so sure?

272
00:17:57,800 --> 00:18:00,430
I know him. He wouldn't do it.

273
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:02,750
How can you trust someone so easily?

274
00:18:11,050 --> 00:18:14,230
[Interrogation Room]

275
00:18:18,490 --> 00:18:22,040
[Interrogation Room]

276
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:25,800
When was the last time you saw the deceased?

277
00:18:29,050 --> 00:18:30,220
In the morning...

278
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:33,480
before he left the condo.

279
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:39,450
Were you two living together?

280
00:18:42,090 --> 00:18:42,790
Yes.

281
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:46,650
We were dating.

282
00:18:51,110 --> 00:18:54,010
Where were you throughout that day?

283
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:01,290
Did you meet the deceased again?

284
00:19:11,210 --> 00:19:12,530
Where were you?

285
00:19:16,110 --> 00:19:16,980
I...

286
00:19:18,940 --> 00:19:20,610
I had something to do at a friend's house.

287
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:28,210
Do you know
where the deceased's phone and laptop are?

288
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,630
I don't.

289
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:33,830
I...

290
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:38,900
searched all over the condo
but couldn't find them...

291
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:41,380
as I already said.

292
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:44,980
Do you know
the phone passcode of the deceased?

293
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:49,770
I do.

294
00:19:51,030 --> 00:19:52,240
He knew mine, too.

295
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:58,490
Do you know
where the deceased's phone and laptop are?

296
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:01,210
I don't know, officer.

297
00:20:01,930 --> 00:20:03,120
I told you already.

298
00:20:03,380 --> 00:20:05,930
Then can you tell me
who the friend you visited that day was?

299
00:20:21,430 --> 00:20:22,580
I can't tell you.

300
00:20:25,790 --> 00:20:28,620
If you provide us
with information that could help,

301
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:31,250
it'll be better for both you

302
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:34,000
and your boyfriend's case.

303
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:35,710
You're aware of that, right?

304
00:20:40,310 --> 00:20:42,400
So why can't you tell us where you were?

305
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:46,150
Personal reasons.

306
00:20:48,430 --> 00:20:49,580
Then can you guess

307
00:20:49,610 --> 00:20:52,210
if anyone else
might be involved in Anda's death?

308
00:20:55,710 --> 00:20:57,340
I really don't know, officer.

309
00:21:16,610 --> 00:21:18,990
Are we really going to meet Kum, Jin?

310
00:21:19,350 --> 00:21:20,350
Yeah.

311
00:21:21,230 --> 00:21:23,220
They're still interrogating him right now,

312
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:25,760
and I don't know when they'll be finished.

313
00:21:26,450 --> 00:21:27,320
I don't know.

314
00:21:27,690 --> 00:21:28,990
It's better than doing nothing.

315
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:32,130
You haven't changed your mind, have you?

316
00:21:32,310 --> 00:21:34,450
Do you still think Kum's not the culprit?

317
00:21:34,820 --> 00:21:36,810
Yeah, I still think so.

318
00:21:40,150 --> 00:21:40,850
Oh...

319
00:21:41,170 --> 00:21:41,950
- Hello.
- Hello.

320
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:43,070
- Hello.
- Hello.

321
00:21:43,090 --> 00:21:44,090
What are you guys doing here?

322
00:21:44,550 --> 00:21:45,890
We've come to see Kum.

323
00:21:45,910 --> 00:21:47,450
Has he left yet?

324
00:21:47,770 --> 00:21:49,020
He's still being interrogated.

325
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:51,340
Why are you guys looking for Kum?

326
00:21:51,370 --> 00:21:52,140
Itti,

327
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:55,450
we're certain that Kum isn't the culprit.

328
00:21:56,310 --> 00:21:57,890
Let the police handle it.

329
00:21:58,340 --> 00:21:59,950
You shouldn't vouch for anyone.

330
00:22:00,130 --> 00:22:01,340
But Itti,

331
00:22:01,790 --> 00:22:05,680
we're actually very close to Kum.

332
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,930
Those two really loved each other.

333
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:10,280
It's impossible.

334
00:22:10,310 --> 00:22:11,430
They were in love.

335
00:22:11,870 --> 00:22:14,850
There's no way
he would hurt Anda like that.

336
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:16,680
But he's not cooperating at all.

337
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:19,270
He's being very suspicious
and won't answer any questions.

338
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:22,670
We haven't been able to let him leave yet.

339
00:22:23,970 --> 00:22:27,610
I think he probably has his reasons,

340
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:31,030
but he definitely wouldn't hurt Anda.

341
00:22:32,030 --> 00:22:33,420
Did Kum and Anda...

342
00:22:34,090 --> 00:22:35,630
ever have any problems?

343
00:22:41,530 --> 00:22:42,310
Hey.

344
00:22:43,370 --> 00:22:45,330
I'll never break up with you, Anda.

345
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:48,220
No matter what, I won't.

346
00:22:48,710 --> 00:22:50,030
They never fought at all.

347
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:52,190
They really loved each other.

348
00:22:53,270 --> 00:22:56,250
Anyway, let the police handle this matter.

349
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:58,350
You guys can go home now.

350
00:23:01,220 --> 00:23:02,500
I'll be going, then.

351
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,460
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

352
00:23:13,550 --> 00:23:14,630
What now?

353
00:23:15,870 --> 00:23:16,750
I don't know.

354
00:23:19,330 --> 00:23:21,810
Art, what on earth are you doing?

355
00:23:21,970 --> 00:23:22,510
Oh...

356
00:23:22,530 --> 00:23:24,370
I've seen you fumbling with that
for a while.

357
00:23:24,510 --> 00:23:26,500
Oh, I was recording.

358
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,370
I saw it in a movie.

359
00:23:28,390 --> 00:23:30,700
They said that no matter what happens,

360
00:23:30,870 --> 00:23:32,140
you should always record it.

361
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:36,990
Record for what?

362
00:23:38,150 --> 00:23:38,790
Well,

363
00:23:39,490 --> 00:23:41,540
it's for evidence.

364
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:43,470
Just in case we miss something,

365
00:23:44,210 --> 00:23:45,840
we can listen to it again.

366
00:23:48,330 --> 00:23:50,690
Does anyone have earphones?
Let me borrow them.

367
00:23:52,130 --> 00:23:55,260
I think I do. Just a sec.

368
00:24:00,790 --> 00:24:01,750
Thanks.

369
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:05,950
One each.

370
00:24:07,010 --> 00:24:08,000
Turn up the volume.

371
00:24:14,840 --> 00:24:16,470
I can't hear a thing, Art.

372
00:24:19,030 --> 00:24:19,810
Yeah.

373
00:24:20,370 --> 00:24:21,520
Are your earbuds broken, Podduang?

374
00:24:21,870 --> 00:24:22,530
What?

375
00:24:23,390 --> 00:24:24,790
How could that be possible?

376
00:24:25,460 --> 00:24:27,310
Dunk just bought me these.

377
00:24:29,150 --> 00:24:30,560
Could it be a knock-off?

378
00:24:31,020 --> 00:24:33,020
In the livestreams I watch,

379
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:35,920
they always sell items that failed QC.

380
00:24:36,210 --> 00:24:37,340
Better be careful.

381
00:24:39,230 --> 00:24:40,860
You complain so much.

382
00:24:41,250 --> 00:24:43,750
You're using someone else's thing,
and you're complaining?

383
00:24:44,470 --> 00:24:46,680
Here, Podduang. Take it.

384
00:24:48,410 --> 00:24:49,210
I have an idea.

385
00:24:49,910 --> 00:24:51,480
I'll put it on the computer in my room

386
00:24:52,070 --> 00:24:54,180
so I can listen to it like a detective.

387
00:24:55,510 --> 00:24:58,170
You're way too into these series.

388
00:24:58,190 --> 00:24:59,180
- Let's go.
- Hey.

389
00:24:59,200 --> 00:24:59,830
Let's go.

390
00:25:00,210 --> 00:25:01,590
See ya. We're heading out.

391
00:25:02,110 --> 00:25:03,800
- See ya.
- See you later.

392
00:25:04,460 --> 00:25:05,640
Let's get going.

393
00:25:07,900 --> 00:25:08,920
I'll give you a ride.

394
00:26:13,990 --> 00:26:15,550
Keep watching the series.

395
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,190
We're reaching the climax.

396
00:26:17,210 --> 00:26:18,350
Oh, are we?

397
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:20,940
- No, that climax.
- We're reaching the climax, right?

398
00:26:22,390 --> 00:26:24,830
- Kum...
- Look, it's almost at the climax.

399
00:26:25,830 --> 00:26:26,730
Kum...

400
00:26:29,090 --> 00:26:30,350
I want us to go public.

401
00:26:30,970 --> 00:26:32,270
It's up to you, Anda.

402
00:26:33,130 --> 00:26:35,690
As for me, I can handle it anyway.

403
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:37,070
See?

404
00:26:38,050 --> 00:26:39,410
You're always like this.

405
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:41,550
How could I not love
this old golden retriever of mine?

406
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:55,180
Anda...

407
00:27:01,140 --> 00:27:02,410
I'm sorry.

408
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:19,910
Anda...

409
00:27:22,150 --> 00:27:23,380
I'm sorry.

410
00:27:26,110 --> 00:27:27,490
I'm really sorry.

411
00:27:36,560 --> 00:27:37,610
I'm sorry.

412
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:46,810
Lieutenant, what do you think
about that Kum guy?

413
00:27:47,580 --> 00:27:49,150
No matter how you look at it, it's strange.

414
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:51,250
If we just had a bit more time,

415
00:27:51,270 --> 00:27:53,310
we could have gotten something from him.

416
00:27:54,110 --> 00:27:55,570
If it wasn't for the law,

417
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:57,420
I wouldn't have let him go.

418
00:27:59,450 --> 00:28:02,390
By the way, aren't you close to him at all?

419
00:28:02,910 --> 00:28:05,430
I heard he's been dating your brother
for a long time.

420
00:28:06,390 --> 00:28:07,250
Not at all.

421
00:28:08,350 --> 00:28:10,020
Anda never brought him to meet me.

422
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,810
They moved out to live together.

423
00:28:12,890 --> 00:28:16,990
But if Kum is involved in Anda's death,

424
00:28:17,350 --> 00:28:19,570
I won't let him get away with it.
You know that, right?

425
00:28:53,600 --> 00:28:54,740
I'm so hungry.

426
00:28:55,420 --> 00:28:56,880
There's nothing to eat in my room.

427
00:28:57,660 --> 00:28:58,610
Do you want anything?

428
00:28:58,940 --> 00:29:00,640
No, you go ahead.

429
00:29:09,140 --> 00:29:10,130
You're really not eating?

430
00:29:10,930 --> 00:29:11,630
Yeah.

431
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:13,700
Then...

432
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:16,530
I'm getting some.

433
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:40,850
What are you looking at?

434
00:29:59,330 --> 00:30:04,660
[Jinna: Can I have your beer?]

435
00:30:21,430 --> 00:30:22,900
I sent you a message.

436
00:30:23,050 --> 00:30:24,050
You didn't reply.

437
00:30:24,070 --> 00:30:25,050
I know.

438
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:27,640
Just a moment.

439
00:30:32,630 --> 00:30:33,640
Why are you giving me this?

440
00:30:34,130 --> 00:30:34,940
What?

441
00:30:41,010 --> 00:30:41,850
Look.

442
00:30:44,840 --> 00:30:46,200
You said you wanted a beer.

443
00:30:46,220 --> 00:30:47,320
[Jinna: Can I have your beer?]

444
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,650
Yeah, a beer it is.

445
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:54,990
But I can't ride home if I drink this.

446
00:30:56,450 --> 00:30:57,490
I know.

447
00:31:03,130 --> 00:31:04,570
I'll drink with you.

448
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:08,660
Get on the bike.

449
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:10,050
What are you standing there for?

450
00:31:10,070 --> 00:31:11,180
Can you hold this?

451
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:11,950
How would I ride the bike?

452
00:31:11,970 --> 00:31:13,410
I need both hands on the handlebar.

453
00:31:17,620 --> 00:31:19,680
Come here, let me put it on for you.

454
00:31:22,830 --> 00:31:25,930
Gotta wear a helmet to stay safe on the road.

455
00:31:27,240 --> 00:31:28,160
Get on.

456
00:31:28,180 --> 00:31:29,450
Here, you go first,

457
00:31:29,600 --> 00:31:30,810
or you won't be able to get on.

458
00:32:00,190 --> 00:32:01,540
Is Satang coming back late again?

459
00:32:02,030 --> 00:32:02,800
Yeah.

460
00:32:03,230 --> 00:32:04,460
He's staying at a friend's house tonight.

461
00:32:05,270 --> 00:32:06,710
I guess they'll be gaming all night again.

462
00:32:08,620 --> 00:32:10,210
He never stays home, does he?

463
00:32:11,110 --> 00:32:13,950
If you see him,
give him a piece of your mind for me.

464
00:32:14,450 --> 00:32:15,840
He really looks up to you.

465
00:32:20,910 --> 00:32:22,730
So, did drinking beer help with the stress?

466
00:32:23,960 --> 00:32:25,390
Why do I have to drink beer
only when I'm stressed?

467
00:32:25,650 --> 00:32:26,690
Why would you think that?

468
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:30,890
Well, you texted me asking for a beer,

469
00:32:30,910 --> 00:32:32,030
so I thought you were stressed.

470
00:32:33,390 --> 00:32:34,860
Oh...

471
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:36,130
It was autocorrect.

472
00:32:38,730 --> 00:32:39,510
Look.

473
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:40,860
[Can I have your numbeer?]

474
00:32:40,880 --> 00:32:43,140
[Can I have your beer?]

475
00:32:43,650 --> 00:32:45,120
Oh...

476
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:48,820
I was wondering
why you suddenly asked for a beer.

477
00:32:49,670 --> 00:32:51,500
I was going to ask for your number.

478
00:32:51,530 --> 00:32:52,390
Number?

479
00:32:53,070 --> 00:32:54,060
Like, my number?

480
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:55,730
Yeah.

481
00:32:57,410 --> 00:32:58,410
What for?

482
00:32:59,370 --> 00:33:00,430
Well, I want it.

483
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:03,340
How many reasons are there
for someone to ask for a number?

484
00:33:04,530 --> 00:33:05,450
Plenty.

485
00:33:06,290 --> 00:33:07,310
You could be trying to sell me insurance.

486
00:33:07,890 --> 00:33:09,220
Or...

487
00:33:10,320 --> 00:33:11,630
